@model ApplicationEditorViewModel
@* Summary: a read-only view of both sections, reusing the same partials (IsReadOnly is true here). *@
@*
    The Summary (4.a.iii - read-only view of both sections, plus Submit).
    It just reuses the two section partials instead of copying their markup, so it always matches them. The service
    sets IsReadOnly = true here, which makes both partials read-only. The Submit button lives in Edit.cshtml, inside
    the one form.
*@
@* Tell the applicant why Submit is greyed out (4.b.ii - both sections have to be saved first). *@
@if (Model.CanEdit && !Model.CanSubmit)
{
    <div class="alert alert-warning">Save both sections before submitting.</div>
}
<partial name="_ApplicantInformation" model="Model" />
<partial name="_ResidenceHistory" model="Model" />
